      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Following a link stays open to anyone on the company network. Nobody wants to sign in just to reach the standup page."
        },
        {
          "text": "Changing links is different. Create, replace or delete, and the API has to know who is asking."
        },
        {
          "text": "It also records who made each link, so there's someone to ask when one breaks.",
          "senses": {
            "records": "verb"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Two kinds of caller: people at a browser, and other services."
        },
        {
          "text": "We start with a service: the release pipeline, run by another team. On every release, it points go slash release-notes at the newest notes.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
