      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "First, a common mix-up. Kubernetes has its own sign-in: your kubeconfig, and RBAC rules on what each user may do."
        },
        {
          "text": "That guards the cluster's API server: who can create a Deployment, or read a Secret. It knows nothing about go links.",
          "senses": {
            "read": "present"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Our product needs its own door. The pipeline calls the go API through Traefik, like any other client, and the API decides. That door uses tokens from Keycloak.",
          "senses": {
            "uses": "verb"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "keycloak",
      "type": "diagram",
      "title": "Keycloak, kept light",
      "boxes": [
        {
          "id": "kc",
          "kind": "group",
          "label": "Keycloak: sso.corp.internal, realm corp",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 90,
          "w": 1480,
          "h": 400
        },
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "label": "client: release-pipeline",
          "sublabel": "an id and a secret",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 200,
          "w": 640,
          "h": 130,
          "tone": "accent",
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "label": "client: golinks",
          "sublabel": "the API that tokens are for",
          "x": 840,
          "y": 200,
          "w": 640,
          "h": 130,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "sc",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "scopes: golinks.write and golinks.read",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 370,
          "w": 1360,
          "h": 80,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "team",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "run by the identity team, outside our cluster",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 560,
          "w": 1480,
          "h": 90,
          "hidden": true
        }
      ],
      "arrows": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
