            "c2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "show": [
            "sc"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Keycloak is an open-source identity server. The company runs it at sso.corp.internal, with one realm, called corp."
        },
        {
          "text": "The identity team runs it, outside our cluster. We only need a few things set up in it, and they're all requests to that team."
        },
        {
          "text": "A client for the release pipeline. It's a confidential client: it gets an id and a secret, which live in the pipeline's own secret store.",
          "senses": {
            "live": "verb"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "A client for golinks itself. Tokens name it as their audience: the service they're meant for."
        },
        {
          "text": "And two scopes, permissions a client can be granted. The pipeline gets golinks dot write. Reading the list needs golinks dot read, which it doesn't have.",
          "say": "And two scopes, permissions a client can be granted. The pipeline gets go links dot write. Reading the list needs go links dot reed, which it doesn't have.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow",
