            "pg",
            "f5"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The flow is called client credentials. The pipeline sends its id and secret to the token endpoint in Keycloak."
        },
        {
          "text": "Keycloak answers with an access token: a JWT, signed by Keycloak, and good for five minutes."
        },
        {
          "text": "The pipeline sends that token to the go API, in an Authorization header."
        },
        {
          "text": "The API checks the signature with the public keys of Keycloak. It fetches them once and caches them, so Keycloak isn't asked on every request."
        },
        {
          "text": "Only then does the change reach Postgres. The secret itself never leaves the pipeline and Keycloak.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "token",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "release pipeline",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "SSO=https://sso.corp.internal/realms/corp/protocol/openid-connect"
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "curl -s -u $CLIENT $SSO/token -d grant_type=client_credentials > t.json"
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "jq '{token_type, expires_in, scope}' t.json",
          "output": [
            "{",
            "  \"token_type\": \"Bearer\",",
            "  \"expires_in\": 300,",
            "  \"scope\": \"golinks.write\"",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "TOKEN=$(jq -r .access_token t.json); echo $TOKEN | tr . '\\n' | cut -c1-60",
          "output": [
            "eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6InE3THIyeEs5Y1dt",
            "eyJleHAiOjE3OTM2MzY3MDQsImlhdCI6MTc5MzYzNjQwNCwiaXNzIjoiaHR0",
            "RXAr7KqFwV52UVeGOQIxNlac1LiayjrFZA0Hw-RDe2OAPZZqBKRCK_Z1IyYL"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Here's the pipeline's side, as plain curl. First, the address that every call to Keycloak starts with."
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask for a token. The client id and secret come from the pipeline's secret store, in CLIENT, and the grant type says which flow this is."
        },
        {
          "text": "The answer: a Bearer token, good for 300 seconds, with the write scope."
        },
        {
          "text": "The token itself is three parts, joined by dots: a header, a payload, and a signature. Each one is base64.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decode",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "release pipeline",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "jq -R 'split(\".\")[1] | @base64d | fromjson' <<< $TOKEN",
          "output": [
            "{",
            "  \"exp\": 1793636704,",
            "  \"iat\": 1793636404,",
            "  \"iss\": \"https://sso.corp.internal/realms/corp\",",
            "  \"aud\": \"golinks\",",
            "  \"sub\": \"4462ebfc-5f91-4ef0-9cfb-ac6e7687a66e\",",
            "  \"typ\": \"Bearer\",",
            "  \"azp\": \"release-pipeline\",",
            "  \"scope\": \"golinks.write\",",
            "  \"preferred_username\": \"service-account-release-pipeline\"",
            "}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Decode the middle part, the payload. These are the token's claims."
        },
        {
          "text": "When it expires, and when it was issued: five minutes apart. Who issued it: our Keycloak realm. And the audience: golinks."
        },
        {
          "text": "The subject is the pipeline's service account in Keycloak, and azp says which client asked for the token.",
          "say": "The subject is the pipeline's service account in Keycloak, and A Z P says which client asked for the token."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the scope it was granted."
        },
        {
          "text": "Anyone holding the token can read all of this, just like base64 in a Secret. It's signed, not encrypted. That's why it only ever travels over HTTPS.",
          "senses": {
            "read": "present"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "checks",
      "type": "diagram",
      "title": "What the API checks, in order",
      "boxes": [
        {
          "id": "k1",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "signature: made with a Keycloak key",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 90,
          "w": 900,
          "h": 80
        },
        {
          "id": "k2",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "iss: https://sso.corp.internal/realms/corp",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 195,
          "w": 900,
          "h": 80,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k3",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "aud: golinks",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 300,
          "w": 900,
          "h": 80,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k4",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "exp: not in the past",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 405,
          "w": 900,
          "h": 80,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "e401",
          "label": "401",
          "sublabel": "who are you?",
          "x": 1140,
          "y": 190,
          "w": 340,
          "h": 130,
          "tone": "bad",
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k5",
          "kind": "note",
          "label": "scope: golinks.write, for PUT and DELETE",
          "x": 120,
          "y": 560,
          "w": 900,
          "h": 80,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "e403",
          "label": "403",
          "sublabel": "not allowed",
          "x": 1140,
          "y": 535,
          "w": 340,
          "h": 130,
          "tone": "warn",
          "hidden": true
        }
      ],
      "arrows": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "focus": [
            "k1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "focus": [],
          "show": [
            "k2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "show": [
            "k3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "show": [
            "k4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "show": [
            "e401"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 5,
          "show": [
            "k5",
            "e403"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So the API checks every token. First the signature. The header names which Keycloak key signed it, so keys can be rotated."
        },
        {
          "text": "The issuer must be exactly our realm."
        },
        {
          "text": "The audience must be golinks. A token Keycloak made for some other service won't work here, even though it's genuine."
        },
        {
          "text": "And it must not have expired. Five minutes is short on purpose: a token that leaks is soon worthless."
        },
        {
          "text": "Fail any of these, and the answer is 401: I don't know who you are."
        },
        {
          "text": "Pass them, and one more check: the scope this route needs. Without it, the answer is 403: I know who you are, and you're not allowed.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cfg-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-configmap.yaml",
      "range": [
        1,
        19
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            14,
            16
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            17,
            19
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The API needs two settings for this, and they've been in its ConfigMap since Episode 3: the issuer URL, and the audience to expect."
        },
        {
          "text": "From the issuer, it finds the public keys of Keycloak on its own: an OIDC discovery document lists where they are."
        },
        {
          "text": "One new line. Keycloak answers over HTTPS, with a certificate from the company CA. The pod has to trust that CA, or it can't fetch the keys at all.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ca-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/corp-root-ca.yaml",
      "range": [
        1,
        23
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            3,
            7
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            11,
            23
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            1,
            2
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So the company root goes in a ConfigMap of its own, corp-root-ca."
        },
        {
          "text": "Its one entry is the root's certificate, the same one company laptops trust."
        },
        {
          "text": "A certificate is public, so unlike the key in Episode 8, this one can live in the repository.",
          "senses": {
            "live": "verb"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "deploy-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-deployment.yaml",
      "range": [
        48,
        71
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            63,
            67
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            68,
            71
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The Deployment mounts it as files. The container gets the folder /etc/corp-ca, read-only.",
          "say": "The Deployment mounts it as files. The container gets the folder slash etc slash corp C A, read-only."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the pod's volumes say where that folder comes from: the ConfigMap. Each key becomes a file, so the API finds ca.crt right where the setting points.",
          "say": "And the pod's volumes say where that folder comes from: the ConfigMap. Each key becomes a file, so the API finds C. A. dot C. R. T. right where the setting points."
        },
        {
          "text": "With many apps, trust-manager, from the cert-manager project, can copy a CA bundle into every namespace for you.",
          "say": "With many apps, trust manager, from the cert-manager project, can copy a C A bundle into every namespace for you.",
          "senses": {
            "project": "noun"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "apply",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl apply -k manifests/base | grep -v unchanged",
          "output": [
            "configmap/corp-root-ca created",
            "configmap/golinks-config configured",
            "deployment.apps/golinks configured"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl rollout status deploy/golinks -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "deployment \"golinks\" successfully rolled out"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Apply the base: a new ConfigMap, a changed one, and a changed Deployment."
